<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to January 6, partly due to a decrease in bank notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   431.50 (+  12.64)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  14.73 (-   6.58)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.18 (+   0.43)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.90 (+   0.08)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 120.65 (+   5.00)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   460.94 (-   7.54)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
